](/wiki/The_Sandman_\(Vertigo\) "The Sandman \(Vertigo\)") _ which had a huge
impact on how characters that are physical embodiments are written in the [
fantasy ](/wiki/Fantasy "Fantasy") genre.  [38]  [39]  Other examples also
include the mature _[ Hellblazer ](/wiki/Hellblazer "Hellblazer") _
(personified political and moral ideas),  [40]  _[ Fables
](/wiki/Fables_\(comics\) "Fables \(comics\)") _ and its spin-off series _[
Jack of Fables ](/wiki/Jack_of_Fables "Jack of Fables") _ , which was unique
for having anthropomorphic representation of [ literary techniques
](/wiki/Literary_techniques "Literary techniques") and [ genres ](/wiki/Genre
"Genre") .  [41]  Various Japanese [ manga ](/wiki/Manga "Manga") and [ anime
](/wiki/Anime "Anime") have used anthropomorphism as the basis of their story.
Examples include _[ Squid Girl ](/wiki/Squid_Girl "Squid Girl") _
(anthropomorphized squid), _[ Hetalia: Axis Powers
