###  Miscellaneous characters  [  [ edit
](/w/index.php?title=Knights_of_the_Dinner_Table&action=edit&section=15 "Edit
section: Miscellaneous characters") ]

The Great Bear Rainforest extends from the [ Discovery Islands
](/wiki/Discovery_Islands "Discovery Islands") in the south to the BC-Alaska
boundary in the north, it includes all offshore islands within this range
except [ Vancouver Island ](/wiki/Vancouver_Island "Vancouver Island") and the
archipelago of [ Haida Gwaii ](/wiki/Haida_Gwaii "Haida Gwaii") .  [1]  Its
northern end reaches up [ Portland Canal ](/wiki/Portland_Canal "Portland
Canal") to the vicinity of [ Stewart ](/wiki/Stewart,_British_Columbia
"Stewart, British Columbia") . To the south it includes [ Prince Rupert
](/wiki/Prince_Rupert,_British_Columbia "Prince Rupert, British Columbia") ,
most of [ Douglas Channel ](/wiki/Douglas_Channel "Douglas Channel") , half of
[ Hawkesbury Island ](/wiki/Hawkesbury_Island "Hawkesbury Island") , and part
of [ Gardner Canal ](/wiki/Gardner_Canal "Gardner Canal") . [ Kitimat
](/wiki/Kitimat,_British_Columbia "Kitimat, British Columbia") is outside the
region, to the east. Farther south, the region includes all of the coast west
and south of the [ Fiordland Conservancy ](/wiki/Fiordland_Conservancy
"Fiordland Conservancy") , [ Kitlope Heritage Conservancy Protected Area
](/wiki/Kitlope_Heritage_Conservancy_Protected_Area "Kitlope Heritage
Conservancy Protected Area") , [ Tweedsmuir North
](/wiki/Tweedsmuir_North_Provincial_Park_and_Protected_Area "Tweedsmuir North
Provincial Park and Protected Area") and [ Tweedsmuir South Provincial Parks
](/wiki/Tweedsmuir_South_Provincial_Park "Tweedsmuir South Provincial Park")
—which includes [ Dean Channel ](/wiki/Dean_Channel "Dean Channel") , [ Burke
Channel ](/wiki/Burke_Channel "Burke Channel") , [ Rivers Inlet
](/wiki/Rivers_Inlet "Rivers Inlet") , and the communities of [ Bella Bella
](/wiki/Bella_Bella,_British_Columbia "Bella Bella, British Columbia") , [
Bella Coola ](/wiki/Bella_Coola,_British_Columbia "Bella Coola, British
Columbia") , and [ Hagensborg ](/wiki/Hagensborg,_British_Columbia
"Hagensborg, British Columbia") . The southern end of the region includes [
Knight Inlet ](/wiki/Knight_Inlet "Knight Inlet") and [ Bute Inlet
](/wiki/Bute_Inlet "Bute Inlet") .  [12]  [13]

