The Great Bear Rainforest is one of the largest remaining tracts of unspoiled
temperate rainforest left in the world.  [14]  The area is home to species
such as [ cougars ](/wiki/Cougar "Cougar") , [ wolves ](/wiki/Gray_wolf "Gray
wolf") , [ salmon ](/wiki/Salmon "Salmon") , [ grizzly bears
](/wiki/Grizzly_bear "Grizzly bear") , and the [ Kermode ("spirit") bear
](/wiki/Kermode_bear "Kermode bear") , a unique subspecies of the [ black bear
](/wiki/American_black_bear "American black bear") , in which one in ten cubs
displays a [ recessive ](/wiki/Dominance_\(genetics\) "Dominance
\(genetics\)") white coloured coat.

